Bearing-only Camera and Scene
===============================================================================
+> math/*

The robot carries a simulated bearing camera. Each row of `landmarks` is a known
point that the camera can observe; `camera-index` chooses that point. The camera
reports its direction relative to the robot's heading, matching the displayed
bearing-only EKF. Measurements are used only within the configured camera range;
outside it, the filter predicts without a bearing correction. This example does
not perform image detection or occlusion.

The browser supplies controls and the accepted filter state. A prepare turn uses
`commit = 0` to calculate measurements without advancing the simulation. After
the filter accepts those measurements, a `commit = 1` turn advances the truth and
trails and publishes the scene. A rejected filter turn leaves these unchanged.

@input := input://browser/frame{
  :read(commit), :read(velocity), :read(omega), :read(noise),
  :read(lane-indices), :read(estimate), :read(covariance), :read(camera-index),
  :read(camera-range)
}
@scene := scene://view/frame{:write(replace)}

Camera Measurements
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  π := 3.141592653589793
  Δt := 0.1
  commit := @input/commit
  landmarks := [140.0 12.0
                 35.0 110.0
                170.0 110.0
                 10.0 10.0]
  camera-position := landmarks[@input/camera-index,:]'
  ~truth := [55.0 25.0 0.4]'
  ~accepted-turns := 0.0
  candidate-truth := truth + Δt * [@input/velocity * cos(truth[3])
                                  @input/velocity * sin(truth[3])
                                  @input/omega]
  camera-offset := camera-position - candidate-truth[1..=2]
  camera-distance := sqrt(camera-offset[1] ^ 2 + camera-offset[2] ^ 2)
  -- A zero/one range gate: include the boundary, with no distance fade.
  camera-range-excess := camera-distance - @input/camera-range
  camera-positive-excess := (camera-range-excess + abs(camera-range-excess)) / 2.0
  measurement-visible := 1.0 - ceil(camera-positive-excess / (abs(camera-range-excess) + 1.0))
  noiseless-bearing := atan2(camera-offset[2], camera-offset[1]) - candidate-truth[3]
  lanes := @input/lane-indices'
  readings := noiseless-bearing + @input/noise * sin((accepted-turns + 1.0) * 1.73 + (lanes - 1.0) * 0.37)
  next-truth := truth + commit * (candidate-truth - truth)
  next-accepted-turns := accepted-turns + commit

Scene Geometry
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

World positions use an upward y axis. The scene transform changes only the
display coordinates; the measurements and filter retain world coordinates.

  estimate := @input/estimate
  covariance := @input/covariance
  screen-origin := [0.0 130.0]'
  screen-axis := [1.0 -1.0]'
  truth-screen := screen-origin + screen-axis * next-truth[1..=2]
  estimate-screen := screen-origin + screen-axis * estimate[1..=2]
  landmark-screen := screen-origin' + landmarks * screen-axis'
  landmark-distance := abs([1.0 2.0 3.0 4.0] - @input/camera-index)
  landmark-selection := (1.0 - landmark-distance + abs(1.0 - landmark-distance)) / 2.0
  landmark-opacity := 0.3 + 0.7 * landmark-selection
  selected-landmark-screen := screen-origin + screen-axis * camera-position
  display-camera-offset := camera-position - next-truth[1..=2]
  display-camera-distance := sqrt(display-camera-offset[1] ^ 2 + display-camera-offset[2] ^ 2)
  display-range-excess := display-camera-distance - @input/camera-range
  display-positive-excess := (display-range-excess + abs(display-range-excess)) / 2.0
  landmark-visible := 1.0 - ceil(display-positive-excess / (abs(display-range-excess) + 1.0))
  camera-ray-opacity := 0.65 * landmark-visible
  truth-heading := truth-screen + 4.3 * screen-axis * [cos(next-truth[3]) sin(next-truth[3])]'
  estimate-heading := estimate-screen + 3.1 * screen-axis * [cos(estimate[3]) sin(estimate[3])]'
  robot-samples := 0.0..=24.0
  robot-angle := robot-samples' * (2.0 * π / 24.0)
  robot-outline := cos(robot-angle ** [1.0 1.0] - [0.0 π / 2.0])
  truth-outline := truth-screen' + 2.6 * robot-outline
  estimate-outline := estimate-screen' + 1.7 * robot-outline
  truth-heading-line := [truth-screen'; truth-heading']
  estimate-heading-line := [estimate-screen'; estimate-heading']
  camera-outline := truth-heading' + 0.6 * robot-outline

The cyan ring marks the actual simulated pose; the smaller yellow disk marks
the EKF estimate. Both remain visible when their positions coincide. A solid
cyan truth path remains visible between the muted-gold estimate trail's dots.
Marker size and heading length affect only the drawing, not either pose.

The position covariance determines the ellipse's axes and orientation. Clamping
tiny negative eigenvalues to zero is a drawing operation, not a filter update.

  ellipse-a := covariance[1,1]
  ellipse-b := (covariance[1,2] + covariance[2,1]) / 2.0
  ellipse-c := covariance[2,2]
  ellipse-root := sqrt(((ellipse-a - ellipse-c) / 2.0) ^ 2 + ellipse-b ^ 2)
  ellipse-eigenvalues := (ellipse-a + ellipse-c) / 2.0 + [1.0 -1.0]' * ellipse-root
  ellipse-nonnegative := (ellipse-eigenvalues + abs(ellipse-eigenvalues)) / 2.0
  ellipse-axes := 2.0 * sqrt(ellipse-nonnegative)
  ellipse-rotation := 0.5 * atan2(2.0 * ellipse-b, ellipse-a - ellipse-c)
  ellipse-samples := 0.0..=64.0
  ellipse-angle := ellipse-samples' * (2.0 * π / 64.0)
  ellipse-phase := ellipse-angle ** [1.0 1.0] - [0.0 π / 2.0]
  ellipse-points := cos(ellipse-phase) * ellipse-axes'
  ellipse-direction := cos(ellipse-rotation - [0.0 π / 2.0])
  ellipse-matrix := [ellipse-direction; -ellipse-direction[2] ellipse-direction[1]]
  covariance-ellipse := estimate-screen' + (ellipse-points ** ellipse-matrix) * screen-axis'

  trail-samples := 1.0..=350.0
  ~truth-path := (trail-samples' * 0.0) ** [1.0 1.0] + [55.0 105.0]
  ~estimate-path := (trail-samples' * 0.0) ** [1.0 1.0] + [55.0 105.0]
  advanced-truth-path := [truth-path[2..=350,:]; truth-screen']
  advanced-estimate-path := [estimate-path[2..=350,:]; estimate-screen']
  next-truth-path := truth-path + commit * (advanced-truth-path - truth-path)
  next-estimate-path := estimate-path + commit * (advanced-estimate-path - estimate-path)

Scene Tables
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The generic scene host draws these tables. Robot geometry, sensor locations,
covariance, and trail history are computed by Mech rather than by the renderer.

  scene-circles :=
    | id<string>   x<f64>               y<f64>               radius<f64> fill<*>  stroke<*> stroke-width<f64> opacity<f64>       |
    | "target-1"   landmark-screen[1,1] landmark-screen[1,2] 1.8         0x62b4a4 "none"    0.0               landmark-opacity[1] |
    | "target-2"   landmark-screen[2,1] landmark-screen[2,2] 1.8         0x62b4a4 "none"    0.0               landmark-opacity[2] |
    | "target-3"   landmark-screen[3,1] landmark-screen[3,2] 1.8         0x62b4a4 "none"    0.0               landmark-opacity[3] |
    | "target-4"   landmark-screen[4,1] landmark-screen[4,2] 1.8         0x62b4a4 "none"    0.0               landmark-opacity[4] |
    | "camera-range" truth-screen[1]   truth-screen[2]      @input/camera-range "none" 0x687780 0.35              0.45               |

  scene-lines :=
    | id<string>    x1<f64>              y1<f64>              x2<f64>                     y2<f64>                     stroke<f64> stroke-width<f64> line-cap<string> opacity<f64> rotation<f64> origin-x<f64> origin-y<f64> |
    | "grid-x-0"    0.0                  0.0                  0.0                         130.0                       0x243139    0.25              "butt"           1.0          0.0 0.0 0.0 |
    | "grid-x-10"   10.0                 0.0                  10.0                        130.0                       0x243139    0.25              "butt"           1.0          0.0 0.0 0.0 |
    | "grid-x-20"   20.0                 0.0                  20.0                        130.0                       0x243139    0.25              "butt"           1.0          0.0 0.0 0.0 |
    | "grid-x-30"   30.0                 0.0                  30.0                        130.0                       0x243139    0.25              "butt"           1.0          0.0 0.0 0.0 |
